# Keep Unix line endings, the norm for PHP and WordPress code.
* text=auto eol=lf
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.zip binary

# Keep development files out of GitHub's "Download ZIP" and out of the tarballs
# attached to a release.
#
# That button is the likeliest way somebody installs this without building it,
# and export-ignore is what makes the result a usable plugin rather than a
# checkout: git archive honours these, and GitHub's archives are git archive.
# A clone is unaffected, so anybody working on the project still gets everything.
#
# .htaccess and the index.php silence files are deliberately NOT listed. They
# are part of what an installation should carry.
/tests           export-ignore
/tools           export-ignore
/docs            export-ignore
/.gitattributes  export-ignore
/.gitignore      export-ignore
